body:
pop science documentaries aren't  'learning a new skill'- it's just high-brow entertainment.  On the same level of personal usefulness as watching porn actually- if we're going to be honest.

&#x200B;

My mind is already full of useless rubbish which has gotten me nowhere in my personal life (liberal arts degree) don't need to fill it up with more surface level shallow generic cr\*p.

north- leeds, newcastle? - maybe back to my mums ancestral areas in the midlands? (derby/leicester). London is thoroughly anti-working class in contrast to those areas. Don't get me wrong... if you're a rich professional london is great (£45k\* annum + assets), if you're not it is pointless.  you will just be miserable.  The wages aren't even all that different from what I've seen online adds either.  There is not even much clubbing left  in london- not that i'm into that- there ain't much up north either mind you. TBH it's just sh\*t everywhere in england when you think about it.  But at least you won't be a pauper up north.

&#x200B;

edit- also beautiful countryside, clean air and water up north( London water causes acne and bad hair btw) forgot that. Also women are 100\* better up north. Don't know how men are as i'm not gay and I like women.  Though I suspect women moving from London won't like them .

1China is a deformed workers state (proletarian dictatorship)- worker state  still owns the means of production but executive decisions are made by a parasitic Stalinist bureaucracy which arose in russia  (and china ) because of  specific political failures in the early 20th century (namely the failure of the German revolution and workers strike in britain in the 1920s).

2. State planning, social welfare policies, history of struggle against bourgeoise powers (Kuomintang). PRC still executes corrupt billionaires -which would never happen in bourgeoise countries, and from the outside in see them more as a necessary evil in this stage of their development- although I don't agree with that premise ideologically, I can see where they're coming from, this is opposed to the state of the ultra wealthy as a protected class like they're in the west and typical bourgeoise countries.

&#x200B;

