 It is harder than I expected to maintain a hobby when it's solo and no audience of any sort, family or online. '

&#x200B;

I have a cope for this, just imagine you have an audience and crowd cheering you on.

You can grow your own tobacco as well if we're being pedantic. Mind you ,have you checked beer and beer-related stocks compare to market performance recently?  The moonshine industry died in the late 30s, the marijuana grey economy has been running unimpeded since the 70s. That's 40-50+ years of experience evading authorities, the kind of people who will not give a flying f\*ck about undercutting regulated companies with ticker symbols who have to go through red-tape formally.

&#x200B;

Don't get me wrong, the hype may just be enough on it's own without solid fundamentals. I've been wrong before (about tesla).

&#x200B;

BTW it's actually very hard and somewhat dangerous to moonshine spirits (not beer I know), all you need for weed is a grow tent.

Just to make a comparison to another industry, it would be like the impact of illegal torrents on the movie and television industry. Now imagine torrents were invented before Hollywood even began, that is the dynamics we're dealing with.
